{"t": 1794114217.856316, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": ":rotating_light: checkout / PaymentGatewayErrors (AG-7731)\n\nWhat happened: gateway 4xx rate hit 38% from 07:41 UTC. Loki shows every charge rejected with 400 `invalid_amount`: \"amount must be an integer in minor units (cents), got 12.34\".\n\nRoot cause: the payment gateway was switched to API version 2026-11 (strict amounts) and now requires `amount` as an integer in minor units. checkout/gateway.py was still sending a float euro amount (e.g. 12.34).\n\nFix: `charge_payload()` now converts EUR to integer cents (Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP): 12.34 EUR -> 1234. Currency stays EUR. Verified locally: 12.34 -> 1234, 19.99 -> 1999, all amounts are ints.\n\nNext: deploy the change and watch the 4xx rate on the gateway dashboard. No other checkout changes were made."}, "ok": true}
